```go
func Get(name string) (Style, error) {
	if style, ok := registryByName[name]; ok { return style, nil }
	return LoadEmbeddedStyle(name)  // ??
}
```

Hmm. Actually I recall chroma v2 has:
```go
var registry = Registry{}
func Get(name string) (Style, error) {
	style, ok := registry[name]
	if !ok {
		return Style{}, fmt.Errorf("...)
	}
}
```

Hmm but the error "open swapoff: no such file or directory" is an *fs.PathError-ish* format from `os.Open`. In chroma v2 there's `styles.Load` / `styles.GetFile`? Let me think: chroma v2 `styles` package has:

```go
// Load loads a style from an XML file.
func Load(path string) (Style, error)
```
And the CLI does something like: if style is a path to XML file, load it; else styles.Get(name).

Actually in chroma v2 CLI (cmd/chroma/main.go):
```go
	style, err := styles.Get(*styleFlag)
